#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:2
msgid "CTest Dashboard Client Guide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:5
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:9
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:11
msgid ""
"A `CDash`_ dashboard collects the results of configuring, building, and "
"testing a project on many machines.  The :manual:`ctest(1)` program acts as "
"a :ref:`Dashboard Client`: it runs those steps and submits the results to a "
"CDash server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:16
msgid ""
"This guide shows how to prepare a project for dashboard submissions, how to "
"submit results from an existing build tree, and how to write a script that "
"runs a dashboard on a schedule.  See the :manual:`ctest(1)` manual for a "
"complete reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:21
msgid ""
"The :ref:`CTest Dashboard Examples` at the end of this guide expand on each "
"topic, one step at a time, with complete scripts that can be run standalone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:28
msgid "Preparing a Project"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:30
msgid ""
"A project enables dashboard submissions by including the :module:`CTest` "
"module in its top-level ``CMakeLists.txt`` file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:33
msgid ""
"cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 4.0)\n"
"project(MyProject)\n"
"\n"
"include(CTest)\n"
"\n"
"if(BUILD_TESTING)\n"
"  add_executable(my_test my_test.cxx)\n"
"  add_test(NAME my_test COMMAND my_test)\n"
"endif()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:45
msgid ""
"The module calls :command:`enable_testing` and adds "
"the :variable:`BUILD_TESTING` option.  It also writes the dashboard settings "
"to a configuration file in the build tree."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:49
msgid ""
"The project also needs a ``CTestConfig.cmake`` file next to its top-level "
"``CMakeLists.txt`` file to say where to submit results.  A CDash server "
"offers this file for download on the settings page of each project. It "
"contains settings such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:54
msgid ""
"set(CTEST_NIGHTLY_START_TIME \"01:00:00 UTC\")\n"
"set(CTEST_SUBMIT_URL \"https://my.cdash.org/submit.php?project=MyProject\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:59
msgid ""
"The :variable:`CTEST_NIGHTLY_START_TIME` variable must match the nightly "
"start time configured in CDash, so that all ``Nightly`` submissions from one "
"night appear on the same day."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:64
msgid "Submitting from a Build Tree"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:66
msgid ""
"The quickest way to submit results is to run :program:`ctest` from an "
"existing build tree.  Configure and build the project as usual, then run an "
"``Experimental`` dashboard:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:70
msgid ""
"cmake -S MyProject -B build\n"
"cmake --build build\n"
"cd build\n"
"ctest -D Experimental"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:77
msgid ""
"This runs the ``Start``, ``Configure``, ``Build``, ``Test``, ``Coverage``, "
"and ``Submit`` steps.  The results are recorded in the ``Testing`` directory "
"of the build tree before they are submitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:81
msgid ""
"The :module:`CTest` module also adds an ``Experimental`` target to the build "
"system that does the same thing:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:84
msgid "cmake --build build --target Experimental"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:89
msgid "Running Individual Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:91
msgid ""
"A dashboard may also be run one step at a time.  The :option:`ctest -M` "
"option selects the mode and each :option:`ctest -T` option adds a step:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:94
msgid "ctest -M Experimental -T Start -T Configure -T Build -T Test -T Submit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:98
msgid ""
"Results are recorded under the tag created by the most recent ``Start`` "
"step, and later invocations add to it.  By default, the ``Submit`` step "
"sends every result recorded under that tag, including results from earlier "
"invocations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:103
msgid ""
"Set :variable:`CTEST_SUBMIT_PARTS` to submit only some of them.  For "
"example, to rerun the tests and submit only the new test results:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:107
msgid "ctest -M Experimental -T Test -T Submit -D CTEST_SUBMIT_PARTS=Test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:111
msgid ""
"See :ref:`CTest Dashboard Step 9` for a complete dashboard run this way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:114
msgid "Overriding Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:118
msgid ""
"Settings in the configuration file can be overridden for one run with "
"the :option:`-D \\<var\\>=\\<value\\> <ctest-dashboard -D>` option.  For "
"example, to submit with a different build name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:122
msgid "ctest -D Experimental -D CTEST_BUILD_NAME=linux-gcc-debug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:127
msgid "Writing a Dashboard Script"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:129
msgid ""
"Machines that submit dashboards on a schedule usually run a script "
"with :option:`ctest -S` instead.  A script can check out the source tree, "
"start from an empty build tree, and choose which steps to run.  It does not "
"depend on a build tree that was configured beforehand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:134
msgid ""
"The script is written in the :manual:`cmake-language(7)`.  It sets variables "
"that hold the dashboard settings and calls the :ref:`CTest Commands` to run "
"each step.  The following script runs a ``Nightly`` dashboard for a project "
"hosted in a Git repository:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:139
msgid ""
"# Describe this machine and build.\n"
"set(CTEST_SITE \"my-machine\")\n"
"set(CTEST_BUILD_NAME \"linux-gcc-release\")\n"
"\n"
"# Choose where to put the source and build trees.\n"
"set(CTEST_DASHBOARD_ROOT \"$ENV{HOME}/dashboards\")\n"
"set(CTEST_SOURCE_DIRECTORY \"${CTEST_DASHBOARD_ROOT}/MyProject\")\n"
"set(CTEST_BINARY_DIRECTORY \"${CTEST_DASHBOARD_ROOT}/MyProject-build\")\n"
"\n"
"# Choose how to configure and build.\n"
"set(CTEST_CMAKE_GENERATOR \"Ninja\")\n"
"set(CTEST_CONFIGURATION_TYPE \"Release\")\n"
"\n"
"# Clone the repository on the first run, and update it later.\n"
"find_program(CTEST_GIT_COMMAND NAMES git)\n"
"set(repo \"https://example.com/MyProject.git\")\n"
"if(NOT EXISTS \"${CTEST_SOURCE_DIRECTORY}\")\n"
"  set(CTEST_CHECKOUT_COMMAND\n"
"    \"\\\"${CTEST_GIT_COMMAND}\\\" clone ${repo} \\\"$"
"{CTEST_SOURCE_DIRECTORY}\\\"\")\n"
"endif()\n"
"\n"
"# Start each night with an empty build tree.\n"
"ctest_empty_binary_directory(\"${CTEST_BINARY_DIRECTORY}\")\n"
"\n"
"ctest_start(Nightly)\n"
"ctest_update()\n"
"ctest_configure()\n"
"ctest_build()\n"
"ctest_test()\n"
"ctest_submit()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:172
msgid "Run the script from any directory outside the build tree:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:174
msgid "ctest -S nightly.cmake -V"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:178
msgid ""
"The :option:`ctest -V` option shows the progress of each step. "
"See :ref:`CTest Dashboard Step 1` for a complete script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:181
msgid "Notes on the script:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:183
msgid ""
"The :command:`ctest_start` command runs "
"the :variable:`CTEST_CHECKOUT_COMMAND`, if set, before it reads "
"``CTestConfig.cmake`` from the binary or source tree. The script does not "
"need to set :variable:`CTEST_SUBMIT_URL` itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:188
msgid ""
"The :command:`ctest_update` command uses :variable:`CTEST_GIT_COMMAND` to "
"update the source tree, and records the changes in the submission."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:191
msgid ""
"The :command:`ctest_configure` command runs :manual:`cmake(1)` with the "
"generator given by :variable:`CTEST_CMAKE_GENERATOR`.  To pass more options "
"to CMake, set :variable:`CTEST_CONFIGURE_COMMAND` or use the ``OPTIONS`` "
"argument of the command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:196
msgid ""
"The :command:`ctest_empty_binary_directory` command does nothing if the "
"build tree does not exist yet.  To avoid removing an unrelated directory by "
"mistake, it fails if the directory exists but does not contain a "
"``CMakeCache.txt`` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:202
msgid "Passing Values to a Script"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:204
msgid ""
"One script can serve several builds by reading values from the command "
"line.  Each :option:`-D \\<var\\>=\\<value\\> <ctest-dashboard -D>` option "
"sets a variable before the script runs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:208
msgid ""
"if(NOT DEFINED CTEST_BUILD_NAME)\n"
"  set(CTEST_BUILD_NAME \"linux-gcc-release\")\n"
"endif()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:214
msgid "ctest -S nightly.cmake -D CTEST_BUILD_NAME=linux-gcc-debug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:218
msgid ""
"Variables whose names do not begin with ``CTEST_`` must be given with a "
"type, such as ``-D dashboard_model:STRING=Nightly``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:221
msgid ""
"Variables whose names begin with ``CTEST_`` may be given without a type. "
"Previously, every variable had to be given with a type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:226
msgid "Continuous Dashboards"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:228
msgid ""
"A ``Continuous`` dashboard runs repeatedly during the day and submits "
"results only when the source tree has changed.  In a script, use the "
"``RETURN_VALUE`` option of :command:`ctest_update` to stop early when "
"nothing changed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:233
msgid ""
"ctest_start(Continuous)\n"
"ctest_update(RETURN_VALUE count)\n"
"if(count EQUAL 0)\n"
"  return()\n"
"endif()\n"
"ctest_configure()\n"
"ctest_build()\n"
"ctest_test()\n"
"ctest_submit()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:245
msgid ""
"A ``Continuous`` script usually keeps its build tree between runs, so it "
"does not call :command:`ctest_empty_binary_directory`.  This keeps each "
"build incremental."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:250
msgid "Checking for Failures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:252
msgid ""
"Each command can store its result in a variable so the script can react to "
"failures.  For example, to skip the tests when the build fails:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:255
msgid ""
"ctest_build(NUMBER_ERRORS errors)\n"
"if(errors EQUAL 0)\n"
"  ctest_test()\n"
"endif()\n"
"ctest_submit()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:263
msgid "See the documentation of each command for the values it reports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:266
msgid "Running on a Schedule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:268
msgid ""
"A dashboard script can be run by the system scheduler (such as ``crontab`` "
"on Linux and macOS), or via a continuous integration platform (such as "
"GitHub Actions).  Schedule ``Nightly`` scripts to start shortly after "
"the :variable:`CTEST_NIGHTLY_START_TIME` so that each submission is "
"associated with the intended day."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:275
msgid "Using CMake Presets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:279
msgid ""
"A project that provides :manual:`cmake-presets(7)` can use them in a "
"dashboard.  In a script, set :variable:`CTEST_PRESET` to use one preset name "
"for the configure, build, and test steps, or "
"set :variable:`CTEST_CONFIGURE_PRESET`, :variable:`CTEST_BUILD_PRESET`, "
"and :variable:`CTEST_TEST_PRESET` separately:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:285
msgid ""
"set(CTEST_SOURCE_DIRECTORY \"${CTEST_DASHBOARD_ROOT}/MyProject\")\n"
"set(CTEST_BINARY_DIRECTORY \"${CTEST_DASHBOARD_ROOT}/MyProject-build\")\n"
"set(CTEST_PRESET \"ci-release\")\n"
"\n"
"ctest_start(Nightly)\n"
"ctest_configure()\n"
"ctest_build()\n"
"ctest_test()\n"
"ctest_submit()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:297
msgid ""
"Settings from the script, such as :variable:`CTEST_BINARY_DIRECTORY`, take "
"priority over the corresponding settings from the preset. See :ref:`CTest "
"Dashboard Step 8` for a complete example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:301
msgid ""
"From the command line, the :ctest-dashboard-option:`--source-dir` option "
"lets the ``Configure`` step create a new build tree from a preset.  If the "
"``ci-release`` preset sets ``binaryDir`` to ``${sourceDir}/build/$"
"{presetName}``, then:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:306
msgid ""
"ctest -M Experimental -T Configure --source-dir MyProject \\\n"
"  -D CTEST_CONFIGURE_PRESET=ci-release\n"
"ctest -M Experimental -T Build -T Test -T Submit \\\n"
"  --test-dir MyProject/build/ci-release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:314
msgid "Adding More Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:317
msgid "Coverage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:319
msgid ""
"To record test coverage, build the project with coverage enabled, such as "
"with the ``--coverage`` flag of GCC, and call :command:`ctest_coverage` "
"after :command:`ctest_test`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:323
msgid ""
"find_program(CTEST_COVERAGE_COMMAND NAMES gcov)\n"
"\n"
"ctest_start(Nightly)\n"
"ctest_configure(OPTIONS \"-DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS=--coverage\")\n"
"ctest_build()\n"
"ctest_test()\n"
"ctest_coverage()\n"
"ctest_submit()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:334
msgid ""
"See the :ref:`CTest Coverage Step` for the supported tools, and :ref:`CTest "
"Dashboard Step 3` for a complete example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:338
msgid "Memory Checking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:340
msgid ""
"To run the tests under a memory checker, call :command:`ctest_memcheck` "
"instead of, or in addition to, :command:`ctest_test`.  "
"The :variable:`CTEST_MEMORYCHECK_TYPE` variable selects the tool:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:344
msgid ""
"set(CTEST_MEMORYCHECK_TYPE \"Valgrind\")\n"
"find_program(CTEST_MEMORYCHECK_COMMAND NAMES valgrind)\n"
"\n"
"ctest_start(Nightly)\n"
"ctest_configure()\n"
"ctest_build()\n"
"ctest_memcheck()\n"
"ctest_submit()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:355
msgid ""
"See the :ref:`CTest MemCheck Step` for the supported tools, including the "
"sanitizers supported by Clang and GCC.  See :ref:`CTest Dashboard Step 4` "
"for complete examples that use AddressSanitizer and Valgrind."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:361
msgid "Detailed Build Reports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:363
msgid ""
"By default, CTest finds build errors and warnings by scanning the build "
"output.  Set :variable:`CTEST_USE_LAUNCHERS` in ``CTestConfig.cmake`` to "
"instead report the command line and output of each compile or link step that "
"produces a warning or error:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:368
msgid "set(CTEST_USE_LAUNCHERS 1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:372
msgid ""
"This works with the :ref:`Makefile Generators` and :ref:`Ninja Generators`. "
"See :ref:`CTest Dashboard Step 2` for a complete example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:376
msgid "Notes and Extra Files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:378
msgid ""
"A submission can include notes files, such as a copy of the dashboard "
"script, to show on CDash.  Set :variable:`CTEST_NOTES_FILES` before "
"calling :command:`ctest_submit`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:382
msgid "set(CTEST_NOTES_FILES \"${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_FILE}\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:386
msgid ""
"From the command line, use the :ctest-dashboard-option:`--add-notes` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/ctest-dashboard-client/index.rst:388
msgid ""
"To attach other files, such as logs or reports, use "
"the :command:`ctest_upload` command.  See :ref:`CTest Dashboard Step 6` for "
"an example."
msgstr ""

